{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact M0 head 0d84b513017325dbf5b403b85542d7110689509b on builder/cross-room-m0-20261108, tree 9c56314f, all nine artifacts, for request f131d4e8 under promise 2b9edaa6 and review request 08b5bacb. That includes the directory artifact at packages. One native test shows a declared v1 send between two rooms with different members. The receiver admits the sender that its genesis names and refuses another verified sender by name. The receiver's member can read the retained source entries and nothing else in the sending room. No production source changes.\n\nThe witness (packages/scope/test/application-cross-room.test.ts and support/cross-room-application.ts):\n\n- Setup:\n  - Rita founds one native register and Vic founds the other, so the two memberships differ, which the test asserts.\n  - Both rooms install the same v1 application through native Rules and Directory installation. The application is defined in the helper.\n  - The receiver's genesis saves `admittedSender` from the installation value.\n- The declared `count` receive guard compares the verified sender with that saved reference and refuses with `not-the-sender`. The helper supplies no replacement check, so native admission makes the decision.\n- The admitted delivery names the sender's exact entry and hash, and the receiver's root takes the count.\n- A second scope runs the same definition and sends the identical message:\n  - The receiver writes exactly one entry: refused, `guard-failed` with `not-the-sender`, no effects and one result send.\n  - The sender receives that refusal.\n  - The receiver's summary is unchanged apart from its time. That meets ruling 99f628a5.\n- The final reads use the receiving membership's real session through the native Worker routes:\n  - Both deciding entries and their retained source entries read 200, and each retained entry equals the exact exported bytes.\n  - Every probed path in the sending room reads 403: the scope, history and entry